Adds a raw byte tunnel mode to the mediated egress broker so a hermetic cell
can make authenticated HTTPS calls (TLS terminated in-cell — keys never reach
the broker in plaintext) while the seal stays HELD: netns still empty, the Unix
socket is the only conduit, (host,port) allowlisted, IP pinned, and the
per-direction ciphertext transcript hash-chained into the signed receipt.
One HTTPS request per tunnel. Enables verifiable autonomous live trading.

